<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wedit (200)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>wedit &lt;someone or something&gt;
wedit &lt;unit@zone&gt;
wedit room
</pre>
<p>An experimental command: it sends a unit's data, as JSON, to your web 
client ("Sending json edit info to your browser."). Name anyone or 
anything in the world, a unit by its symbolic name (the name alone looks 
in your own zone), or room for the room you are in. It only works in the 
web client.
</p><p>For now the client only writes the data to the browser's console (open 
the browser's developer tools to see it). The long-term goal is an 
editor in the web client, for editing units with a good content editor.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Set</a>
</pre>




</div>